course: dictionary
lesson: 1527
title: A bird's cere
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name small parts of animals, and you can work out what they mean from the words around them. «You can usually tell an adult male budgie from a female by the cere, the bare patch above the beak.» The clues are bare patch and above the beak.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put «the bare patch above the beak» in place of cere and the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
explain: The sentence also gives colour clues: the cere is often blue in males and brown or pale in females. So a cere is not just any bit of skin. It can change colour, and that colour can tell you something about the bird.
fact: Cere means the soft, waxy, often brightly coloured patch of skin at the top of a bird's beak.
fact: The cere sits around the nostrils, the two holes a bird breathes through.
fact: Birds with a cere include parrots, budgies, hawks and pigeons.
fact: In a budgie, a blue cere often means male, and a brown or pale cere often means female.
fact: «Young budgies have stripes on their foreheads that fade as they grow», so the cere is a better clue for telling adult budgies apart.
exercise: What is a cere? | *A soft, waxy patch of skin at the top of a bird's beak | The hard tip at the end of a beak | A small cage for budgies | A long feather on a bird's tail
exercise: «You can usually tell an adult male budgie from a female by the cere.» Which bird is this sentence about? | Eagle | *Budgie | Goldfish | Rabbit
exercise: Ayla says a cere is a bird's tail feather. Is she right? | *No, it is a soft, waxy patch of skin at the top of the beak | Yes, it is a long tail feather | Yes, it is the bird's song | No, it is a kind of seed
test: A budgie with a blue cere is often which sex? | Female | Young | *Male | Sick
test: Which word means the soft, waxy patch at the top of a bird's beak? | Crest | *Cere | Feather | Talon
exam: Which statement about a cere is true? | *It is found in birds such as parrots, budgies, hawks and pigeons | It is a sound a bird makes | It is found only in fish | It is a type of grass
